  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Public goods funding refers to mechanisms that finance resources which are non-excludable and non-rival \u2014 meaning consumption by one party does not diminish availability to others and exclusion is impractical. In decentralised ecosystems, on-chain coordination primitives such as quadratic funding, retroactive grants, and DAO-managed treasuries are used to allocate capital towards open-source software, protocol research, and shared infrastructure. These mechanisms attempt to correct the market failure of under-provision that arises when contributors cannot capture sufficient private value from their public-benefit work.",
